Z||000000||The Aura||12-05-2001||03:44 PM||||Are the GM crate motors any good. There web site says 160 horsepower and 200 ft/lbs, but thats with a carb. What kind of hp and torque #'s would it get with a crane compucam, fiero intake and injector system, headders and a bored out fiero TB? Is 220 obtainable?<P>------------------<BR>1986 GT 4spd&gt; Suspension Techniques Springs, Poly Bushings, Bosal Brospeed 4.5" Exhaust Tips, Cross Drilled Rotors||||reg||7
Z||000001||My7Fieros||12-05-2001||09:20 PM||||Yes its obtainable. Here's the deal though...<BR>(From my understanding) only the 93-95 3.4s (Camaro/Firebird engines) are an "exact" match. By that I mean that those engines can be not only installed w/o any mods into a Fiero (only exception being the starter must be moved to the other side of the block, but thats it), but you can also use the Fiero upper intake plenum and valve covers on it. When finished it will look like a stock Fiero V6.<BR>As far as "crate engines being any good"..of course...they're brand new GM engines! Also keep in mind (Ed Parks of the Fiero Factory told me this, but I knew it already) that GM has always been "modest" about the h.p. #'s they give on their engines.....namely due to insurance reasons. They have done this for years and years.<BR>Ive driven Ed Parks 85 Se w/ a 3.4 in it. Only mods he did was remove the stock exhuast manifolds and put on headers. I can tell you, that thing had some SERIOUS zip to it. No,not blindingly fast, but very very peppy. Ive def considered doing the swap.<BR>So 220 horses should be no prob whatsoever. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroRacer||12-06-2001||04:22 PM||||If I need a new block for Demon, I'm going to have a friend pick up a 3.4 Camaro engine from the Junkyard he has access to.  We're going to re-cam it, put new pistons and rings, maybe stroke it, and toss it in.  Why pay for another 2.8 when I could build up a 3.4.  Did I mention this friend has built race engines and used to work in a pit crew?  Mean GT!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||12-06-2001||04:26 PM||||That's definitely the way to go cost-wise.  It was cheaper for me to build a 3.1L using my old 2.8 parts, than to get a new 2.8! (at the time the 3.4's were new & expensive)<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula||12-07-2001||12:07 AM||||I have a 3.4 crate with the stock intake, valve covers and injectors.<P>its a lot stronger then the 2.8.||||reg||1
